  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1: Introduction",
  "nextTour": "2: Set Up Auth0 and Run Z-Assistant",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Welcome to the Lab",
      "description": "## Welcome to the Lab\n\nIn this lab you will work with **Z-Assistant**, an AI-powered customer service agent for **RetailZero** — a fictitious e-commerce platform.\n\nZ-Assistant helps customer service representatives:\n- Look up orders and customer information\n- Browse the product catalog\n- Process refunds on behalf of customers\n- Access full customer profiles (including contact and payment details)\n\nThe catch? Without proper authorization controls, Z-Assistant can autonomously execute sensitive operations like refunds and expose private customer data — all without any human oversight."
    },
    {
      "title": "What You Will Build",
      "description": "## What You Will Build\n\nYou will progressively add security controls to Z-Assistant using **Auth0 for AI Agents**:\n\n1. **Standard Tool Calling** — Connect Z-Assistant to RetailZero's internal API for safe operations (order lookup, product browsing).\n\n2. **Human-in-the-Loop Authorization (CIBA)** — Protect sensitive operations (refunds, customer PII) with **Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication**. Before Z-Assistant can process a refund or access private data, it will send an out-of-band approval request to the user's device. The agent can only proceed once the human approves.\n\nThis pattern ensures your AI agent can never autonomously execute high-risk operations, even if it receives a malicious instruction."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Security Problem",
      "description": "## The Security Problem\n\nWithout authorization controls, a customer service rep could accidentally (or an attacker could intentionally) prompt Z-Assistant to:\n\n> *\"Process a full refund for all of Sarah's orders.\"*\n\n> *\"Show me the payment details for every Gold-tier customer.\"*\n\nA naive AI agent would execute these requests immediately. With **CIBA**, every sensitive action requires explicit human approval — the agent initiates an authorization request, the user reviews and approves on their registered device, and only then does the agent proceed.\n\nThis is the **human-in-the-loop** security pattern for AI agents."
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites",
      "description": "## Prerequisites\n\nYou will need:\n\n1. An **Auth0 account** (free tier is fine) — [sign up here](https://auth0.com/signup) if you don't have one.\n2. An **OpenAI API key** — [get one here](https://platform.openai.com/signup).\n3. For CIBA (Tour 5): the **Auth0 Guardian** mobile app installed on your phone.\n\nThat's it — no third-party API credentials required. RetailZero's API is included in this repository."
    },
    {
      "title": "Get an OpenAI API Key",
      "file": "z-assistant/.env.local",
      "description": "## Get an OpenAI API Key\n\n1. Sign up or log in at [platform.openai.com](https://platform.openai.com/signup).\n2. Go to the **API keys** section of your dashboard.\n3. Select **Create new secret key** and name it **Z-Assistant lab**.\n4. Copy the key and paste it as the value for `OPENAI_API_KEY` on the highlighted line above.\n\n> **Note:** You will need billing credits on your OpenAI account. Set up billing under the gear icon → Billing.",
      "line": 1,
      "selection": {
        "start": { "line": 1, "character": 17 },
        "end": { "line": 1, "character": 29 }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites Complete!",
      "description": "## Prerequisites Complete!\n\nYou now have everything you need. Let's move on to running Z-Assistant and connecting it to Auth0."
    }
  ]
}
